  "chapter": {
    "number": 27,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(28) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "To you, O Lord, have I cried; my God, be not silent toward me: lest you be silent toward me, and so I should be likened to them that go down to the pit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Listen to the voice of my supplication, when I pray to you, when I lift up my hands toward your holy temple.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Draw not away my soul with sinners, and destroy me not with the workers of iniquity, who speak peace with their neighbors, but evils are in their hearts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Give them according to their works, and according to the wickedness of their devices: give them according to the works of their hands; render their recompense to them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because they have not attended to the works of the Lord, even to the works of his hands, you shall pull them down, and shall not build them up.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed be the Lord, for he has listened to the voice of my petition.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is my helper and my defender; my heart has hoped in him, and I am helped: my flesh has revived, and willingly will I",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 50
          },
          {
            "text": "give praise to him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord is the strength of his people, and the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 51
          },
          {
            "text": "saving defender of his anointed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Save your people, and bless your inheritance: and take care of them, and lift them up for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 50,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, confess to him.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 27,
          "verse": 7
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 51,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. defender of the salvation of.",
        "reference": {
